  "body": "## Summary\n\n**Data Lake capacity ladder + migration fixes** (first commit):\n- Data Lake deposit capacity now climbs the same plain decade-power-of-10 shape pool Capacity uses (1 KB → 10 KB → 100 KB → 1000 KB), replacing an 11-level SI-clean sequence.\n- Fixes two migration gaps an automated review pass (Devin) found on the now-merged PR #544 (decade-power pool Capacity): a saved pool buffer or Data Lake `capacityLevel` from before that change could sit above the new, lower bounds. `normalizePoolMemoryCapacity` (runs on every save load) now clamps both.\n- A locally-scoped variable rename (`unlockedPoolCount` → `visiblePoolCount`) and a latent test-seed fix, both from the same review.\n\n**Storage reveal threshold + Data Lake panel redesign + Dev Mode fix** (second commit, per further maintainer requests):\n- `isStorageUnlocked`'s own `INTRO_DISK_UNLOCK_CAPACITY` moves from 80,000 bits (\"9.765 KiB\") to 8,192 bits (\"1 KiB\") — now expressed as `BITS_PER_BYTE * MEMORY_BINARY_UNIT_STEP`, the same product pool 1's own card-visibility gate computes — so the whole Storage section and pool 1's card reveal at the exact same instant, with pool 1 already showing a clean \"1 KB\" Capacity rather than one that had already advanced to \"10 KB\" by the time a player first saw it. The read-cache pre-fill mechanic (from #544) needed no code change — it was already wired through the same gate.\n- `DataLakePanel` redesigned from a dense grid table (explicit Lake/Deposited/Capacity/Bought/Next column headers) to one self-contained block per lake — title row + a big `FillableStatCard` deposited/capacity number + a compact actions row — mirroring the same visual language every other Byte Foundry balance already uses (`FillableStatCard`/`BalanceText`/`StatusText`). Each lake's visible name now includes its size unit (\"KB Lake,\" not just \"KB\").\n- A follow-up adversarial review round found that Dev Mode's Variables-tree \"Set\" editor (`setDevState`) bypassed `normalizePoolMemoryCapacity` entirely, unlike the other two Dev Mode write paths — a manual `capacityLevel` edit there could still trigger the out-of-bounds read the first commit otherwise fixed. `setDevState` now runs its result through the same clamp before committing.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `yarn test`: 1630/1630 green.\n- [x] `yarn build` succeeds.\n- [x] Ran and published the `simulate-run-times` skill (career + PP + capacity-cap sweeps) twice — once per commit — since both touch Byte Foundry economy formulas; pacing is essentially unchanged (Storage's own reveal threshold doesn't gate the main-game-unlock path, which is driven by a separate, earlier constant).\n- [x] Verified visually via `yarn dev` + real Playwright/Chromium screenshots: a from-scratch save seeded at exactly 1 KiB Capacity shows Storage/pool 1 revealed with a clean \"1 KB\" Capacity; the redesigned Data Lake block renders correctly standalone and alongside a second, larger pool.\n- [x] A new test drives the actual Dev Mode Variables-tree UI (expand → type an out-of-range value → Set) to confirm `setDevState`'s own clamp fires, not just `applyDevStateJson`'s (already-correct) path.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [x] `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/ECONOMY_REFERENCE.md`, `docs/MAINPAGE_REFERENCE.md`, `docs/COMPONENTS_REFERENCE.md`, `docs/DESIGN_HISTORY.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md` all updated in the same commits as the code they describe.\n\nTracking issue: #543.\n",
